A||||5||rockcrawl||Disapointing mention of the Fiero in Car Collector magazine||||13||
Z||000000||rockcrawl||05-19-2001||10:00 PM||||I was browsing through the January 2001 issue of Car Collector magazine that was part of the "goodie bag" that was handed out to all Carlisle show participants. I was excited when I came to a feature titled "The 20th Century Automoble" and saw a small picture of a Fiero among others. I quickly turned to the 1981-1990 section where there is a 1/3 page picture of an '85 GT and a caption that reads: "In the 1980's Pontiac gave us the Fiero, then <B>fortunately</B> took it away. It was a good idea that never reached its full potential before dwindling sales killed it off." <P>The guy that wrote that (Dennis Adler) must be a real idiot. If the car had not yet reached its full potential, why is it fortunate that they took it away. I don't quite understand that one. Wouldn't it have been more fortunate for them to continue production for a few more years and perfect it? Needles to say, the Fiero did not make it onto their "most desireable cars" or "100 greatest cars" list.||||reg||13
Z||000001||Fformula88||05-19-2001||10:48 PM||||Sounds like he's been reading Mr. Davis's editorials out of Automobile Magazine.  Most likely he is a big Chevy guy and loves Vettes, and couldn't stand the thought of a V8 Fiero blowing the doors of his beloved Vettes  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||sjp777||05-19-2001||11:18 PM||||The problem with Vettes is that they got about 1000 pounds of engine and fiberglass sitting over the front wheels. Now if Chevy was smart, the would redesign the vette and put the engine behind the passenger compartment.<P>But then they would just have a bitchin Fiero wouldn't they?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_1.jpg">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
